Nautilus DevOps: AWS ECR Containerized Application Deployment
This document records the steps, implementation details, and verification results for creating an Amazon Elastic Container Registry (ECR) repository and pushing a containerized application image using the aws-client host.

1. Overview & Objectives
Task: Create a private ECR repository named devops-ecr in the us-east-1 region.

Build Source: Build a Docker image from the Dockerfile located at /root/pyapp on the aws-client host.

Image Tag: Tag the built image as latest and push it to the newly created ECR repository.

2. Implementation Steps
Step 2.1: Configure AWS CLI Region & Verify Identity
Log in to the aws-client host, verify credentials, and set the default region to us-east-1:

Bash
aws configure set region us-east-1
aws sts get-caller-identity
Step 2.2: Create the Private ECR Repository
Create the private ECR repository with scan-on-push enabled:

Bash
aws ecr create-repository --repository-name devops-ecr --image-scanning-configuration scanOnPush=true --region us-east-1
Step 2.3: Authenticate Docker with ECR
Retrieve the temporary authorization token and authenticate the local Docker client:

Bash
aws ecr get-login-password --region us-east-1 | docker login --username AWS --password-stdin 796938193522.dkr.ecr.us-east-1.amazonaws.com
Step 2.4: Build, Tag, and Push the Docker Image
Navigate to the application directory, build the image, tag it with the ECR repository URI, and push it:

Bash
cd /root/pyapp
docker build -t devops-ecr:latest .
docker tag devops-ecr:latest 796938193522.dkr.ecr.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/devops-ecr:latest
docker push 796938193522.dkr.ecr.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/devops-ecr:latest
